    "body": "The goal is to align `packspec` documentation with how it is being used in `vim.pack` (the primary client implementation, I assume). In particular:\n\n- Describe the structure as it is used in `vim.pack`.\n- Replace usage of \"package\" with \"plugin\". Not a strong opinion, but those are different things and `vim.pack` is aimed to be a plugin manager (i.e. not for system packages, CLI tools packages, LSP servers packages, etc.).\n\n---\n\nWhile working on this, I noticed that `vim.pack` doesn't mention `version` field of `pkg.json`. Mostly because it is not really needed, as versions are assumed to be done via properly named Git tags. But also because the main `TL;DR` example didn't have it :)\n\nShould `packspec` still have definition for the `version` field or is it better to leave as is with Git tags? If the former, should `vim.pack` mention it in the `:h vim.pack-manifest`, although it will not have any usage there?",
    "closed_at": null,
